{"id":31359621883,"name":"Windows Build Validation","node_id":"WFR_kwLORJ3s7s8AAAAHTS3a-w","head_branch":"master","head_sha":"dedc280bc5b8cbf19aeb07c105612073fe401f0d","path":".github/workflows/windows-validation.yml","display_title":"Windows Build Validation","run_number":120,"event":"schedule","status":"completed","conclusion":"cancelled","workflow_id":289954087,"check_suite_id":85057233573,"check_suite_node_id":"CS_kwDORJ3s7s8AAAATzc5ipQ","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ipswitch8/PDFE/actions/runs/31359621883","html_url":"https://github.com/ipswitch8/PDFE/actions/runs/31359621883","pull_requests":[],"created_at":"2026-08-10T05:45:37Z","updated_at":"2026-08-10T17:58:27Z","actor":{"login":"ipswitch8","id":23087562,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMDg3NTYy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/23087562?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ipswitch8","html_url":"https://github.com/ipswitch8","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ipswitch8/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ipswitch8/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ipswitch8/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ipswitch8/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ipswitch8/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ipswitch8/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ipswitch8/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ipswitch8/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ipswitch8/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"run_attempt":1,"referenced_workflows":[],"run_started_at":"2026-08-10T05:45:37Z","triggering_actor":{"login":"ipswitch8","id":23087562,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMDg3NTYy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/23087562?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ipswitch8","html_url":"https://github.com/ipswitch8","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ipswitch8/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ipswitch8/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ipswitch8/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ipswitch8/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ipswitch8/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ipswitch8/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ipswitch8/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ipswitch8/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ipswitch8/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"jobs_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ipswitch8/PDFE/actions/runs/31359621883/jobs","logs_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ipswitch8/PDFE/actions/runs/31359621883/logs","check_suite_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ipswitch8/PDFE/check-suites/85057233573","artifacts_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ipswitch8/PDFE/actions/runs/31359621883/artifacts","cancel_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ipswitch8/PDFE/actions/runs/31359621883/cancel","rerun_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ipswitch8/PDFE/actions/runs/31359621883/rerun","previous_attempt_url":null,"workflow_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ipswitch8/PDFE/actions/workflows/289954087","head_commit":{"id":"dedc280bc5b8cbf19aeb07c105612073fe401f0d","tree_id":"ab08ddb188d449a25a54228020b1afc5bdf817a9","message":"fix(signatures,ui): stop saying \"Validated\" about a signature nothing trusts (F52+F53+F59, phase-50)\n\nF52. A document signed with a self-minted certificate and shipped with\nno /DSS displayed as \"Validated (no revocation data)\". The digest\nverifies -- over the attacker's own bytes -- the chain reaches no anchor,\nand verify() DELIBERATELY rewrote UntrustedChain -> NoDssData, whose\ndisplay string begins with the word \"Validated\". The honest text existed\nin result.message and MainWindow discarded it one call later.\n\nThe rewrite is gone. The digest result and the trust result no longer\nshare a word: \"Signature intact -- certificate NOT trusted\", with the\nreason on a detail row that now actually reaches the panel.\n\nUSER DECISION, taken knowingly: people who deliberately use self-signed\ncertificates will see a warning where they saw \"Validated\". That cost is\nstated unsoftened in the decision record. The wording IS the fix.\n\nF53. A forged responder and \"no revocation data\" rendered identically --\nrogue OCSP, unauthorised CRL, expired/future/delta CRL, stale response,\nmalformed blob all collapsed to one verdict. New status\nRevocationEvidenceRejected, plus the rejecting rule in result.message.\n\nTHE FIRST ATTEMPT AT F53 ACCUSED HONEST DOCUMENTS, and the non-gate\nsecurity review PROVED IT BY EXECUTION. crlAuthorityFor() returns None\nfor two unrelated situations: the CRL is forged, and the CRL is\nperfectly genuine but simply is not about the signer. A document\ncarrying long-term validation material has a CRL per chain link, so the\nroot's CRL -- covering the intermediate -- hit the second case EVERY\nTIME. A fully-covered, entirely valid document was told a CRL \"failed\nissuer authorisation\"; it hadn't. One with partial coverage was told\n\"Revocation evidence REJECTED\", the string introduced to mean something\nadversarial is happening. Same shape on the OCSP side, where the\nauthorisation check runs before OCSP_resp_find_status() establishes the\nresponse is even about this certificate.\n\nThat is the same species as this branch's own HEAD commit, which stopped\naccusing missing files of being malicious. Fixed by gating the\nDIAGNOSTIC note on a relevance predicate -- no security check moved or\nweakened, the artifact is discarded either way. The predicate needed\nwidening once in flight: DN-match OR asserts indirectCRL reddened\nNonIndirectCrlFromAncestorCannotSpeakForLeaf, because an ancestor CRL\nrevoking the signer without declaring itself indirect claims coverage\nthrough its ENTRIES. Final: DN match OR crlEntryRevokesCert().\n\nWHY THE TESTS MISSED IT, which is the transferable part: the F53\npositive control supplied exactly ONE CRL. It was clean, honest, and\nstructurally incapable of witnessing the defect. A positive control for\na CLASSIFICATION must contain a distractor -- otherwise it proves only\nthat the classifier does not misfire on an empty room.\n\nF59. The revokedPathCert walk kept running full signature verifications\nafter finding a revoked CA. Fixed. The committed crl_chain corpus is\nroot -> intermediate -> leaf, so the walk has exactly ONE link and could\nnot have witnessed an early break IN EITHER DIRECTION; the test mints a\nfour-level chain in memory and asserts linkVisits == 2 on the\nnot-revoked run, so == 1 is not merely measuring a short path.\n\nThree more from the review, all fixed: the \"compiler-enforced\nexhaustive\" claim for ltvStatusToDisplayString() was FALSE -- no\n-Wswitch/-Werror anywhere in a PDFE-owned CMake file, and a trailing\nreturn tr(\"Unknown\") acting as a de facto default. Now enforced with\nwarning(error: 4062) (the 3: is required, C4062 is off by default) and\nproved by deleting a case and watching the build fail. The rejection\nreason is appended to the UntrustedChain message rather than dropped.\nQt::PlainText on the new label, so a future message carrying user data\ncannot fake a second status line.\n\nDisclosed, not papered over: hasValidCrlForCert() requires Direct while\nisCertRevokedByCrl() accepts Indirect, so an ancestor indirect CRL is\ngood enough to revoke you but not to vouch for you. Reporting that\nrefusal would falsely accuse an honest document -- the exact defect\nabove -- so it is documented instead.\n\nA standing control caught the work in progress: PadesDocClaims went RED\nbecause \"PAdES B-LT\" was written into two src/ comments and PDFE does\nnot implement PAdES. Reworded. The guard was right.\n\nGates: karen, validator, security-audit, test-runner -- all PASS; karen\nand validator each re-ran a mutation themselves and reproduced the\nrecorded RED sets. Suite 5524 -> 5534 / 0 failures / 8 skipped (tests ==\npassed + skipped, parsed from the XML, never the exit code); the 8\nenumerated, none of them LTV, CRL, OCSP, TSA, DSS or signature. Build\nwarning-clean. Gate-checker suite 507. DCA 17/17.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","timestamp":"2026-08-10T05:30:10Z","author":{"name":"ipswitch8","email":"23087562+ipswitch8@users.noreply.github.com"},"committer":{"name":"ipswitch8","email":"23087562+ipswitch8@users.noreply.github.com"}},"repository":{"id":1151200494,"node_id":"R_kgDORJ3s7g","name":"PDFE","full_name":"ipswitch8/PDFE","private":true,"owner":{"login":"ipswitch8","id":23087562,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMDg3NTYy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/23087562?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ipswitch8","html_url":"https://github.com/ipswitch8","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ipswitch8/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ipswitch8/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ipswitch8/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ipswitch8/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ipswitch8/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ipswitch8/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ipswitch8/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ipswitch8/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ipswitch8/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"html_url":"https://github.com/ipswitch8/PDFE","description":null,"fork":false,"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ipswitch8/PDFE","forks_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ipswitch8/PDFE/forks","keys_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ipswitch8/PDFE/keys{/key_id}","collaborators_url":"https://